(Lee Je Hoon)

00:00:20.965 --> 00:00:22.995
(Jang Hyuk Jin, Bae Yoo Ram, Kim Eui Sung, Pyo Ye Jin)

00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:37.144
(Taxi Driver 3)

00:00:37.145 --> 00:00:38.245
(This drama is a work of fiction)

00:00:38.315 --> 00:00:39.385
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds...)

00:00:39.445 --> 00:00:40.455
(in this drama are fictitious.)

00:00:40.515 --> 00:00:41.785
(Children and animals were filmed under guidelines.)

00:00:45.155 --> 00:00:47.995
(Episode 2)

00:01:08.945 --> 00:01:12.145
Goodness. I told that old fool to take it easy.

00:01:16.055 --> 00:01:18.285
- Has she paid off her debt? - Yes, sir. She's paid in full.

00:01:26.595 --> 00:01:28.395
At least put some clothes on her.

00:01:28.765 --> 00:01:29.765
Understood.

00:01:30.305 --> 00:01:31.305
All right.

00:01:35.975 --> 00:01:37.775
You're still alive?

00:01:39.105 --> 00:01:40.105
How pathetic.

00:01:41.345 --> 00:01:43.215
Must be tough, right?

00:01:46.645 --> 00:01:48.455
She was stabbed with a wine opener.

00:01:49.185 --> 00:01:52.885
On her upper body alone, we found 29 stab wounds.

00:01:53.185 --> 00:01:54.455
There are 29 wounds?

00:01:54.995 --> 00:01:56.355
So she was murdered with a wine opener?

00:01:56.965 --> 00:01:58.125
The cause of death was asphyxiation.

00:01:59.195 --> 00:02:00.535
From the ligature marks here,

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:03.065
it appears she was strangled with a pair of blue stockings.

00:02:03.535 --> 00:02:06.235
The issue is how the body was displayed,

00:02:06.365 --> 00:02:07.835
almost as if to make a statement.

00:02:08.575 --> 00:02:10.005
Gosh, this is gruesome.

00:02:14.545 --> 00:02:17.245
- Let me know if you find any leads. - Will do.

00:02:18.585 --> 00:02:19.585
Look at this.

00:02:23.485 --> 00:02:25.825
Her fingerprints and footprints have been erased,

00:02:26.625 --> 00:02:28.455
so we can’t confirm her identity yet.

00:02:29.395 --> 00:02:31.465
But we think she’s the woman...

00:02:31.495 --> 00:02:33.395
who went missing in Hong Kong two years ago.

00:02:35.135 --> 00:02:36.135
Yes.

00:02:36.635 --> 00:02:37.635
It's her.

00:02:39.635 --> 00:02:41.175
Forensics suggest...

00:02:41.435 --> 00:02:43.475
it doesn’t seem like they tried to hide anything.

00:02:44.305 --> 00:02:45.745
They left her here on purpose.

00:02:46.645 --> 00:02:47.745
Just like they’re saying,

00:02:48.945 --> 00:02:51.585
"Here she is, come get her."

00:02:52.115 --> 00:02:53.115
Yes.

00:02:53.215 --> 00:02:54.255
It's getting bolder.

00:02:55.155 --> 00:02:56.155
More frequent too.

00:03:03.355 --> 00:03:04.365
Go ahead.

00:03:06.025 --> 00:03:07.595
What? They got hit?

00:03:09.965 --> 00:03:14.775
(Taxi Driver 3)

00:03:20.515 --> 00:03:21.515
(Closed, Authorized Personnel Only)

00:03:23.315 --> 00:03:25.745
(Closed, Authorized Personnel Only)

00:03:29.485 --> 00:03:31.125
- Get to work! - Yes, sir!

00:04:04.955 --> 00:04:08.355
- This job will take forever. - Oh, great. Two more people.

00:04:08.455 --> 00:04:09.825
Hey, get some coffee over here too.

00:04:09.995 --> 00:04:12.265
Don't go playing favorites with your buddies.

00:04:31.445 --> 00:04:32.445
Here, sir.

00:04:32.945 --> 00:04:35.715
Boss should be satisfied with these sales numbers.

00:04:53.505 --> 00:04:56.775
Profits from Korea and Hong Kong are up from the last quarter.

00:04:59.005 --> 00:05:00.005
Give them a bonus.

00:05:01.075 --> 00:05:03.745
Hard work must be rewarded.

00:05:04.515 --> 00:05:06.045
Understood, boss.

00:05:09.885 --> 00:05:13.085
My apologies, sir. Some guy suddenly started a brawl,

00:05:13.385 --> 00:05:14.725
so we couldn't finish selecting the security detail.

00:05:16.825 --> 00:05:18.965
He's the one who caused the scene at the gym.

00:05:19.465 --> 00:05:20.565
The reason?

00:05:20.935 --> 00:05:22.565
Apparently, someone spit on his shoes.

00:05:31.245 --> 00:05:32.745
Tell your boss.

00:05:34.545 --> 00:05:35.615
To buy me new shoes,

00:05:37.185 --> 00:05:38.215
and when he does,

00:05:39.785 --> 00:05:40.785
have him call me here.

00:05:41.955 --> 00:05:44.485
Well, well. It seems we were at fault.

00:05:45.425 --> 00:05:48.025
Buy him a new pair of shoes and set up a meeting.

00:05:49.525 --> 00:05:51.265
When you're wrong,

00:05:52.425 --> 00:05:53.425
you apologize.

00:05:54.065 --> 00:05:55.135
Understood.

00:05:58.965 --> 00:06:01.935
They hold monthly fight clubs to recruit...

00:06:02.035 --> 00:06:04.305
the people they need for their organization.

00:06:04.905 --> 00:06:06.075
But how did you figure that out?

00:06:06.775 --> 00:06:08.075
It was on a whiteboard.

00:06:15.285 --> 00:06:17.085
So that means we found a solid lead, right?

00:06:17.385 --> 00:06:18.925
More like you've set the perfect bait.

00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:26.625
Chief Choi.

00:06:26.925 --> 00:06:28.465
Go straight through the intersection.

00:06:28.865 --> 00:06:30.035
What? What's going on?

00:06:31.405 --> 00:06:32.935
We're being followed.

00:06:33.165 --> 00:06:34.175
What?

00:06:35.875 --> 00:06:37.445
How do you want us to back you up?

00:06:38.005 --> 00:06:41.215
I'm good. It's just one car.

00:06:41.515 --> 00:06:44.285
You think it's those guys from the gym?

00:06:44.585 --> 00:06:46.545
Guess I'll have to ask them in person.

00:07:16.375 --> 00:07:17.585
You want to go for round two...

00:07:18.545 --> 00:07:19.545
right here?

00:07:23.885 --> 00:07:26.485
- Gosh! My bad, my bad. - You're just too big.

00:07:27.755 --> 00:07:29.295
I'm Detective Suzuki of the Fukuoka Prefectural Police.

00:07:39.605 --> 00:07:41.205
You're coming with us.

00:07:41.505 --> 00:07:42.805
Come on.

00:07:43.235 --> 00:07:45.475
(Fukuoka Prefectural Police Headquarters)

00:07:46.075 --> 00:07:47.415
This makes no sense.

00:07:51.985 --> 00:07:54.615
How does a Korean get his hands on a Japanese taxi?

00:07:57.115 --> 00:07:59.585
- It was given to me. - Answer me in Japanese.

00:07:59.855 --> 00:08:02.325
Other than a taxi company,

00:08:03.395 --> 00:08:04.625
where else can you get a taxi?

00:08:04.925 --> 00:08:06.725
Hey. You don't realize the trouble you're in, do you?

00:08:08.935 --> 00:08:11.905
Let me guess. You're really, really mad at me?

00:08:14.135 --> 00:08:16.935
- Why, you little punk! - I'm so scared.

00:08:25.585 --> 00:08:26.585
Hello?

00:08:27.415 --> 00:08:29.285
Kim Do Gi?

00:08:32.485 --> 00:08:35.425
That's right. He's here on a special training program from our company.

00:08:36.695 --> 00:08:37.695
Yes.

00:08:39.095 --> 00:08:40.525
I'll fax it over to you.

00:08:41.365 --> 00:08:42.365
Okay.

00:08:45.935 --> 00:08:49.505
- Thank you for your help. - Of course. It was no trouble.

00:09:01.655 --> 00:09:03.485
It checks out. What he said is true.

00:09:03.885 --> 00:09:05.484
He’s also listed as an employee...

00:09:05.485 --> 00:09:07.725
of a South Korean company called Rainbow Taxi.

00:09:09.895 --> 00:09:11.525
Who is this guy?

00:09:11.625 --> 00:09:12.864
Shows up out of nowhere...

00:09:12.865 --> 00:09:15.265
and ruins everything we’ve been working on for months.

00:09:16.435 --> 00:09:18.505
We should get him deported immediately.

00:09:23.505 --> 00:09:24.575
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:25.005 --> 00:09:27.145
If, as you say,

00:09:28.415 --> 00:09:29.945
he ruined our operation,

00:09:30.215 --> 00:09:32.685
burned through our funds, and wasted our time.

00:09:34.115 --> 00:09:35.255
Then logically,

00:09:36.415 --> 00:09:38.155
he might be the only option we have left.

00:09:38.655 --> 00:09:41.195
What? How does that make any sense?

00:09:44.225 --> 00:09:45.225
Lunchbox.

00:09:55.805 --> 00:09:56.805
Excuse me.

00:10:00.645 --> 00:10:01.875
Care for a cup of coffee?

00:10:03.875 --> 00:10:04.885
I know a place.

00:10:20.295 --> 00:10:21.335
Michael Chang.

00:10:21.965 --> 00:10:23.035
Interpol Inspector.

00:10:23.435 --> 00:10:25.105
You know Interpol, right?

00:10:25.705 --> 00:10:26.805
He's the real deal.

00:10:27.635 --> 00:10:29.875
First the police, and now Interpol.

00:10:29.935 --> 00:10:31.945
Feels like I'm in some serious trouble.

00:10:32.975 --> 00:10:34.575
We’re making him feel worried.

00:10:35.415 --> 00:10:36.775
Of course he’d feel that way.

00:10:37.745 --> 00:10:38.915
Sorry if I offended you.

00:10:39.315 --> 00:10:40.885
He says he's sorry.

00:10:41.055 --> 00:10:42.055
Sure you are.

00:10:42.355 --> 00:10:43.355
You understand English?

00:10:44.015 --> 00:10:47.025
I get the feeling you’ve got something specific you want to say.

00:10:48.995 --> 00:10:50.055
What? You speak it fluently too?

00:10:54.695 --> 00:10:56.165
Have you ever seen this game before?

00:10:59.535 --> 00:11:01.005
Over the past three years,

00:11:02.075 --> 00:11:05.075
more and more people from Hong Kong, Taiwan,

00:11:05.575 --> 00:11:08.545
and other parts of Asia have gone missing after coming to Japan.

00:11:09.915 --> 00:11:12.915
Hey, isn't that the gambling game I Seo and I played?

00:11:13.645 --> 00:11:15.085
And they all have a few things in common.

00:11:18.625 --> 00:11:21.155
They all borrowed money from a loan company called Neko Money,

00:11:22.425 --> 00:11:23.425
failed to repay it,

00:11:24.525 --> 00:11:25.525
came to Japan,

00:11:26.425 --> 00:11:27.425
and then vanished.

00:11:29.465 --> 00:11:31.105
And this gambling game...

00:11:31.865 --> 00:11:32.865
is where they all began.

00:11:33.865 --> 00:11:34.875
Are you serious?

00:11:35.475 --> 00:11:39.805
So these jerks run the same scam in other countries too.

00:11:40.605 --> 00:11:42.075
Matsuda Keita.

00:11:43.015 --> 00:11:44.145
Owns a loan company.

00:11:45.785 --> 00:11:48.785
Also a key player in the crime gang that's been rising in this region.

00:11:49.255 --> 00:11:50.385
That gym you visited?

00:11:51.325 --> 00:11:54.425
Matsuda uses it as a recruitment hub for his organization.

00:11:55.155 --> 00:11:56.355
And the opponent you knocked down?

00:12:01.565 --> 00:12:04.095
He was actually one of our undercover officers.

00:12:04.535 --> 00:12:05.665
After a few tests,

00:12:06.265 --> 00:12:09.075
he was set to be selected as Matsuda’s security today.

00:12:14.345 --> 00:12:15.645
Why are you telling me all this?

00:12:16.575 --> 00:12:18.485
Matsuda likes trained fighters.

00:12:19.285 --> 00:12:22.355
Especially someone exceptionally skilled in combat.

00:12:23.885 --> 00:12:24.885
You’d be a great help.

00:12:27.155 --> 00:12:29.125
And what makes you think I'd help you?

00:12:31.425 --> 00:12:32.595
You show up in Japan,

00:12:33.525 --> 00:12:35.035
walk into Matsuda’s gym,

00:12:35.965 --> 00:12:36.965
pick a fight,

00:12:37.765 --> 00:12:40.235
and take down one of our biggest guys easily.

00:12:41.235 --> 00:12:43.475
And you’re telling me you’re just a taxi driver?

00:12:44.745 --> 00:12:47.875
Come on. Even you would admit that sounds a little off.

00:12:51.885 --> 00:12:53.885
I'm not going to ask who you really are...

00:12:54.755 --> 00:12:57.355
or why you're trying to get close to this guy.

00:12:58.255 --> 00:13:00.125
As long as it benefits both of us,

00:13:02.925 --> 00:13:03.925
that's all that matters.

00:13:09.235 --> 00:13:10.235
Thanks for the drink.

00:13:16.735 --> 00:13:20.005
The more I see him, the more suspicious he looks.

00:13:20.475 --> 00:13:22.215
A trilingual taxi driver?

00:13:23.015 --> 00:13:24.885
Where in the world do you find someone like that?

00:13:26.715 --> 00:13:27.715
Right there.

00:13:33.085 --> 00:13:35.295
What are you going to do if this all goes south?

00:13:36.055 --> 00:13:37.325
What about damage control?

00:13:37.525 --> 00:13:39.965
Damage control is something you do after things go wrong.

00:13:40.895 --> 00:13:41.935
Let’s think about it then.

00:13:46.005 --> 00:13:48.335
Please, try some. Welcome.

00:13:48.475 --> 00:13:51.075
Gosh, Driver Kim Do Gi is a trouble magnet, even out here.

00:13:52.275 --> 00:13:55.275
But is it really okay for us to get involved in a police case?

00:13:55.745 --> 00:13:57.245
It's not exactly ideal.

00:13:58.215 --> 00:13:59.545
However, as things stand,

00:13:59.915 --> 00:14:03.315
it's worth seeking common ground that helps us both.

00:14:04.015 --> 00:14:06.485
And I think it might help us find I Seo too.

00:14:07.255 --> 00:14:08.255
I agree.

00:14:09.425 --> 00:14:12.825
Looks like I Seo is in with someone far more dangerous than we thought.

00:14:13.395 --> 00:14:15.495
First, meeting this guy they call the boss...

00:14:15.765 --> 00:14:17.735
- is the top priority. - Exactly.

00:14:20.505 --> 00:14:21.505
Hey!

00:14:21.605 --> 00:14:24.445
We got a customer. See, Chief? Told you we should've charged more.

00:14:24.605 --> 00:14:25.605
I don't speak Japanese.

00:14:26.705 --> 00:14:28.515
When did this place get here?

00:14:30.575 --> 00:14:32.845
Should I go bring some customers here?

00:14:33.015 --> 00:14:34.455
Welcome!

00:14:34.655 --> 00:14:37.415
How about five dollars per head?

00:14:37.455 --> 00:14:38.455
Welcome!

00:14:39.985 --> 00:14:41.025
Are you messing with me?

00:14:41.595 --> 00:14:42.595
Welcome.

00:14:42.596 --> 00:14:45.765
Do you have any idea who I am?

00:14:46.995 --> 00:14:50.395
I'm the man who served...

00:14:50.635 --> 00:14:53.505
the original owner of this land.

00:14:53.665 --> 00:14:56.875
The third-generation leader of the Haneshima Clan,

00:14:57.705 --> 00:14:59.775
Hoshino Masahisa.

00:15:02.315 --> 00:15:03.615
When I walked down the street,

00:15:04.345 --> 00:15:06.945
no one even dared to breathe.

00:15:07.785 --> 00:15:08.954
Welcome.

00:15:08.955 --> 00:15:10.315
If I so much as heard...

00:15:10.985 --> 00:15:13.055
so much as a breath,

00:15:13.955 --> 00:15:16.825
it was off with their heads!

00:15:18.195 --> 00:15:19.395
That's the man I am.

00:15:22.435 --> 00:15:25.765
He wants a cut for bringing clients. Just tell him yes.

00:15:26.835 --> 00:15:30.475
- Okay! Good. Okay. - Okay. Five dollars per head.

00:15:30.535 --> 00:15:31.575
Okay! Yes, okay!

00:15:31.675 --> 00:15:33.975
Okay! You should've just said so in the first place.

00:15:34.545 --> 00:15:37.375
Let's make this work. All right.

00:15:50.095 --> 00:15:51.965
What a long-winded way to say he's shaking us down.

00:15:52.125 --> 00:15:54.395
What was that? He just comes in here acting like he owns the place.

00:15:54.665 --> 00:15:56.894
He's probably just some washed-up yakuza.

00:15:56.895 --> 00:15:59.504
Gosh, I guess our little shop has a sales rep now.

00:15:59.505 --> 00:16:01.235
Salesman? He's just a thug.

00:16:01.735 --> 00:16:03.035
Someone's mad. Why?

00:16:06.875 --> 00:16:07.945
Hello?

00:16:10.675 --> 00:16:11.685
Right. Yes.

00:16:13.185 --> 00:16:17.255
If the new shoes are ready, it's time to go break them in.

00:16:20.625 --> 00:16:22.555
Looks like I'll finally meet this so-called boss.

00:16:28.195 --> 00:16:30.635
We've been expecting you. This way, please.

00:16:56.055 --> 00:16:58.195
Have a seat.

00:17:04.765 --> 00:17:05.835
I'll apologize.

00:17:07.435 --> 00:17:08.435
Formally.

00:17:10.205 --> 00:17:12.245
So that's him? The boss?

00:17:18.315 --> 00:17:20.315
My old shoes, indeed.

00:17:23.585 --> 00:17:24.855
Now it's your turn.

00:17:26.055 --> 00:17:28.255
You caused a disturbance on our turf.

00:17:28.995 --> 00:17:30.555
So it's only right that you apologize.

00:17:32.565 --> 00:17:34.365
- Ikuya. - Yes, sir.

00:17:50.745 --> 00:17:52.715
I've apologized your way.

00:17:53.445 --> 00:17:55.885
So now, you will apologize my way.

00:17:57.785 --> 00:17:58.785
It's only fair.

00:18:00.725 --> 00:18:02.725
And how would you like me to apologize?

00:18:03.555 --> 00:18:04.565
Leave one of your fingers behind,

00:18:06.725 --> 00:18:08.565
and I'll accept your apology.

00:18:28.115 --> 00:18:29.115
Don't like that idea?

00:18:34.255 --> 00:18:35.995
If you're skilled enough, come and take it.

00:19:40.255 --> 00:19:41.825
So you're the boss here?

00:19:46.625 --> 00:19:48.135
I do want to apologize, though.

00:19:54.635 --> 00:19:56.875
Do you accept a finger from someone else?

00:20:04.615 --> 00:20:05.945
Please spare me, boss!

00:20:17.325 --> 00:20:18.325
Boss!

00:20:18.395 --> 00:20:21.125
Driver Kim Do Gi. They're here sooner than we thought.

00:20:23.995 --> 00:20:25.265
Time out.

00:20:47.655 --> 00:20:50.095
Get out of the way unless you want to be arrested too!

00:20:56.435 --> 00:20:57.895
What? He already bolted?

00:21:06.045 --> 00:21:07.705
And here I thought those uninvited guests were for me.

00:21:08.075 --> 00:21:09.375
Turns out they were here for you?

00:21:09.675 --> 00:21:12.785
Since I owe you one, does that mean I owe you a finger?

00:21:14.715 --> 00:21:16.585
A killer from Korea.

00:21:17.085 --> 00:21:18.925
I knew you weren't some average joes, but still.

00:21:20.325 --> 00:21:22.325
You think you have something on me now?

00:21:23.395 --> 00:21:26.495
You're not important enough to have a weakness.

00:21:26.725 --> 00:21:29.265
All the powerless punks I've seen are just like you.

00:21:30.235 --> 00:21:32.505
They are all bark and no bite.

00:21:32.735 --> 00:21:37.235
- That's it. That's all I'm taking. - Time out, time out.

00:21:38.105 --> 00:21:42.315
- See? You're all talk. - Hey, what did you just say?

00:21:42.775 --> 00:21:44.115
Say it so I can understand!

00:21:44.615 --> 00:21:48.285
- Blah, blah. - Hey. Stop the car.

00:21:49.455 --> 00:21:50.455
Stop the car.

00:21:52.585 --> 00:21:53.585
Stop the car!

00:21:54.925 --> 00:21:56.225
That's right, don't stop.

00:21:57.255 --> 00:21:59.225
- Stop. - Yes, sir.

00:21:59.865 --> 00:22:01.535
- Don't stop. - Stop!

00:23:33.155 --> 00:23:34.255
Darn it.

00:23:41.965 --> 00:23:44.035
I was about to make you...

00:23:44.835 --> 00:23:48.105
get me some water. Guess there's no need now.

00:24:02.855 --> 00:24:04.055
Did he hit his head or something?

00:24:11.765 --> 00:24:14.495
You've got a decent punch. Though you're still no match for me.

00:24:17.565 --> 00:24:18.665
You want another round?

00:24:21.335 --> 00:24:24.105
You got nowhere to go? Why don't you work for me?

00:24:25.645 --> 00:24:29.875
What, so you can cut off my finger? I'll pass.

00:24:30.815 --> 00:24:32.245
Forget the finger.

00:24:33.015 --> 00:24:34.015
Work for me.

00:24:38.015 --> 00:24:39.055
No.

00:24:44.095 --> 00:24:45.095
Thanks for the water.

00:24:49.095 --> 00:24:51.335
Hey. Work for me.

00:25:09.555 --> 00:25:10.885
Welcome!

00:25:11.485 --> 00:25:12.485
Thank you.

00:25:14.725 --> 00:25:17.395
This is tough. Really tough.

00:25:17.795 --> 00:25:19.425
Something is actually hard for you, Go Eun?

00:25:21.265 --> 00:25:24.795
I've hacked into every company Matsuda supposedly runs,

00:25:24.835 --> 00:25:27.565
but it looks like all the important data is analog.

00:25:27.965 --> 00:25:30.005
This whole network is just a shell.

00:25:30.935 --> 00:25:33.245
And there's not one clue about I Seo.

00:25:34.575 --> 00:25:36.315
Am I missing a server?

00:25:46.255 --> 00:25:48.225
It's like you said, Go Eun. It won't be on a server.

00:25:49.595 --> 00:25:52.125
He doesn't seem like the type to trust even his own people.

00:25:52.595 --> 00:25:56.295
The key data is probably somewhere he keeps from his own people.

00:25:57.995 --> 00:26:01.705
Criminal groups usually operate as a cell network,

00:26:02.375 --> 00:26:06.305
but this Matsuda fellow doesn't seem to trust his own cells.

00:26:06.745 --> 00:26:10.815
On the bright side, that means we only have one person to handle.

00:26:11.015 --> 00:26:13.215
Looks like you'll have to meet with him more often.

00:26:13.315 --> 00:26:14.785
- Hey! - It's hot.

00:26:17.585 --> 00:26:19.455
For crying out loud. He's here again?

00:26:19.525 --> 00:26:21.455
Does he have to show up almost every single day?

00:26:21.655 --> 00:26:24.755
The guy I sent earlier was here, right?

00:26:25.125 --> 00:26:26.565
Welcome.

00:26:26.965 --> 00:26:28.265
The fee. Five dollars.

00:26:30.565 --> 00:26:31.565
Darn it.

00:26:35.705 --> 00:26:36.705
What's this?

00:26:37.775 --> 00:26:39.145
I said five dollars.

00:26:39.245 --> 00:26:43.074
Wait. If a customer pays 10 dollars and ingredients cost 5 dollars,

00:26:43.075 --> 00:26:45.345
and your fee is five dollars, how are we meant to make a living?

00:26:45.715 --> 00:26:49.085
- See? Five dollars won't work! - What was that?

00:26:49.855 --> 00:26:51.925
I'm the man who served the original owner of this land.

00:26:52.385 --> 00:26:54.585
The third-generation leader of the Haneshima Clan,

00:26:55.225 --> 00:26:56.494
Hoshino Masahisa.

00:26:56.495 --> 00:26:57.555
How dare you?

00:26:58.125 --> 00:27:00.795
You dare speak to me like that!

00:27:01.625 --> 00:27:04.935
Give it to him and get rid of him before he starts on his glory days.

00:27:05.135 --> 00:27:07.035
No, no. This is completely unfair.

00:27:08.105 --> 00:27:10.305
I've heard that story so many times. My ears are bleeding.

00:27:15.715 --> 00:27:16.915
That's more like it.

00:27:21.045 --> 00:27:23.915
Hey, wait! My one dollar! You have to give me my change! Hey!

00:27:24.085 --> 00:27:25.485
Just let it go. Don't pick a fight.

00:27:25.825 --> 00:27:27.985
On my way here, I saw many guys like him on the main street...

00:27:28.055 --> 00:27:29.595
That guy comes here often.

00:27:30.025 --> 00:27:31.525
He can't get a job,

00:27:32.125 --> 00:27:35.395
let alone a credit card. Even his bank accounts are frozen.

00:27:35.695 --> 00:27:38.035
It's like he's living in the past, not the present.

00:27:46.205 --> 00:27:47.845
Hey, you piece of trash!

00:27:48.575 --> 00:27:49.845
What are you doing hanging around here?

00:27:51.215 --> 00:27:54.044
What, feeling nostalgic for your old turf?

00:27:54.045 --> 00:27:57.255
Actually, I can't hear you.

00:27:58.015 --> 00:28:01.325
Here! Go hole up in a temple and die already.

00:28:01.385 --> 00:28:02.755
Old geezer!

00:28:03.895 --> 00:28:06.225
Sorry. That sounds good.

00:28:09.165 --> 00:28:10.565
Oh, you're playing dumb?

00:28:13.205 --> 00:28:17.105
Aren't those the guys who were in front of the gym?

00:28:45.965 --> 00:28:48.305
You're not waiting for me to get you one, are you?

00:28:48.875 --> 00:28:51.405
Funds from the foreign branches have started moving rapidly.

00:28:51.905 --> 00:28:53.575
That means Matsuda is planning something.

00:28:58.415 --> 00:28:59.415
We don't have time.

00:29:00.145 --> 00:29:01.545
We need to come up with a plan.

00:29:02.755 --> 00:29:03.755
A plan?

00:29:04.055 --> 00:29:05.285
You have something in your mind?

00:29:06.855 --> 00:29:08.055
We need to get inside them.

00:29:12.265 --> 00:29:14.695
I was thinking of getting some food.

00:29:15.335 --> 00:29:16.335
Food?

00:29:16.895 --> 00:29:17.895
But to eat,

00:29:19.505 --> 00:29:20.805
I'll need that guy's help.

00:29:28.245 --> 00:29:29.615
What are you looking at?

00:29:33.515 --> 00:29:36.185
How many units did they say are coming in today?

00:29:38.385 --> 00:29:40.255
Four from the Far East.

00:29:40.625 --> 00:29:44.325
Eight from Central, plus two others. We're expecting ten in total.

00:29:44.695 --> 00:29:45.965
So that's 14 in total.

00:29:47.265 --> 00:29:49.395
A toast, everyone?

00:29:50.065 --> 00:29:51.065
- Cheers. - Cheers.

00:29:54.305 --> 00:29:57.075
As always, I appreciate all your hard work.

00:29:57.705 --> 00:30:00.405
It's for you, Matsuda. Of course we'll do our best.

00:30:02.575 --> 00:30:04.175
And another thing.

00:30:05.345 --> 00:30:06.715
Don't mistake me for a fool.

00:30:07.645 --> 00:30:08.655
I'm not sure what you mean.

00:30:13.055 --> 00:30:15.085
All that cash you've been pocketing...

00:30:16.195 --> 00:30:17.725
Don't think for a second I didn't know.

00:30:41.545 --> 00:30:42.715
You backstabbing traitor.

00:31:01.165 --> 00:31:03.435
What kind of driving is that?

00:31:07.145 --> 00:31:08.305
Who do you think you are?

00:31:08.875 --> 00:31:11.415
You interested in finding out who I am?

00:31:21.225 --> 00:31:22.425
If you're that curious,

00:31:23.055 --> 00:31:25.125
why don't we discuss it over tea?

00:31:26.325 --> 00:31:28.395
Hey, this isn't what you promised!

00:31:31.595 --> 00:31:32.605
What are you staring at?

00:31:33.135 --> 00:31:34.135
What are you staring at?

00:31:35.335 --> 00:31:36.375
Go mind your business!

00:31:46.515 --> 00:31:47.545
Who is it?

00:31:53.185 --> 00:31:54.355
Can you even make a living doing that?

00:31:57.055 --> 00:31:58.495
A man needs to make a living.

00:31:59.025 --> 00:32:00.525
So move your car.

00:32:15.345 --> 00:32:16.875
Hey!

00:32:19.715 --> 00:32:20.745
Nice work.

00:32:20.945 --> 00:32:22.285
Nice work?

00:32:22.785 --> 00:32:25.055
Is this really the right way to handle this?

00:32:26.025 --> 00:32:27.785
Because it feels like he's just messing with us,

00:32:27.885 --> 00:32:29.125
rather than helping us.

00:32:30.795 --> 00:32:31.995
Leave me out of that "us."

00:32:35.895 --> 00:32:38.195
I haven't even eaten all day.

00:32:43.205 --> 00:32:44.705
- This is delicious. - It's tasty.

00:32:46.875 --> 00:32:48.045
I told you. It's my treat.

00:32:48.815 --> 00:32:52.115
You got it last time, so it's my turn.

00:32:53.785 --> 00:32:57.615
If you insist. I'll be sure to eat a lot, then.

00:32:57.915 --> 00:33:00.125
Sure. Eat up.

00:33:00.825 --> 00:33:03.325
Just don't have more than three.

00:33:09.565 --> 00:33:13.105
I haven't had many fares today, so I'm a bit short on cash.

00:33:13.505 --> 00:33:14.735
What's that, no money?

00:33:15.935 --> 00:33:16.935
Hey, you.

00:33:17.305 --> 00:33:20.905
Look, it can't be helped. It's on the house. We're closing up!

00:33:21.475 --> 00:33:22.975
- What? - Hey, I said we're closing!

00:33:41.795 --> 00:33:43.165
For over ten years,

00:33:44.395 --> 00:33:46.665
I did every kind of dirty job imaginable.

00:33:47.735 --> 00:33:49.805
While we were taking down a rival crew,

00:33:50.175 --> 00:33:52.175
my guys, who were like brothers to me,

00:33:52.945 --> 00:33:54.605
betrayed me and my boss.

00:33:56.545 --> 00:33:58.675
I lost my crew and my boss,

00:33:59.485 --> 00:34:01.285
but I made sure every one of them paid.

00:34:02.285 --> 00:34:03.415
Backstabbers like them...

00:34:04.385 --> 00:34:05.755
They don't deserve to live.

00:34:07.625 --> 00:34:08.625
Even these shoes...

00:34:10.295 --> 00:34:12.265
They were the last gift my boss ever gave me.

00:34:17.595 --> 00:34:19.165
Quit driving a taxi and come work for me.

00:34:21.505 --> 00:34:26.075
Don't worry about rival crews. I wiped them all out long ago.

00:34:26.845 --> 00:34:28.205
I'll pay you ten times what you make as a taxi driver.

00:34:30.575 --> 00:34:31.575
I'm not interested.

00:34:32.545 --> 00:34:34.785
What will it take for you to join my crew?

00:34:35.445 --> 00:34:39.085
I don't serve two bosses.

00:34:40.285 --> 00:34:41.585
You're a stubborn one.

00:34:42.025 --> 00:34:43.025
But...

00:34:43.625 --> 00:34:45.125
I could do some freelance work.

00:34:47.465 --> 00:34:49.365
Especially if it involves getting my hands dirty.

00:34:50.065 --> 00:34:51.235
Because that's what I'm good at.

00:34:53.965 --> 00:34:58.505
We're Invisible, so for big jobs, we use disposable people.

00:34:58.575 --> 00:34:59.575
That's why we use freelancers.

00:35:01.475 --> 00:35:02.645
So... You into young women?

00:35:07.145 --> 00:35:08.145
Young women?

00:35:09.885 --> 00:35:12.625
I have many undocumented girls you can treat like slaves.

00:35:13.625 --> 00:35:14.785
Want one as a gift?

00:35:18.995 --> 00:35:19.995
Is he seriously...

00:35:20.295 --> 00:35:22.365
talking about the people they kidnapped?

00:35:23.165 --> 00:35:25.435
A gift? Those murdering jerks.

00:35:28.805 --> 00:35:29.905
What? You don't want one?

00:35:33.845 --> 00:35:35.675
Any man who'd gratefully accept a woman as a gift,

00:35:36.345 --> 00:35:39.545
he's the first one you should get rid of.

00:35:40.645 --> 00:35:42.185
That's the kind of person...

00:35:42.955 --> 00:35:44.385
you can never trust.

00:35:48.755 --> 00:35:50.325
You even turn me down in style.

00:35:51.995 --> 00:35:54.225
I get paid in cash.

00:35:55.965 --> 00:35:56.965
Done.

00:36:19.925 --> 00:36:21.525
Hey, hey, over here.

00:36:22.025 --> 00:36:25.155
Okay, okay. Excuse us! Yes.

00:36:25.665 --> 00:36:29.495
- All right! Hey! - Okay.

00:36:32.905 --> 00:36:35.305
Okay. That's good. Looks good.

00:36:42.205 --> 00:36:43.715
Hey, freelancer.

00:36:51.585 --> 00:36:54.485
While the deal's going down, you all watch the perimeter.

00:36:55.655 --> 00:36:59.195
When we're done, you pull out. You've got the back door.

00:37:00.165 --> 00:37:01.265
And if anyone crashes the party,

00:37:01.665 --> 00:37:02.895
I just crush them, right?

00:37:04.935 --> 00:37:07.235
The less you have to do, the smoother everything's going.

00:37:07.865 --> 00:37:08.865
Do your job well.

00:37:27.255 --> 00:37:28.455
Yes, it's a beautiful night, isn't it?

00:37:28.785 --> 00:37:30.555
Not that we can see anything in the dark.

00:37:31.795 --> 00:37:33.025
Shall we get right to it?

00:37:41.705 --> 00:37:43.935
She's 168cm, size 2.

00:37:44.435 --> 00:37:46.545
This lovely lady is from Russia.

00:37:46.845 --> 00:37:48.775
So when they talked about auctioning off "merchandise,"

00:37:49.515 --> 00:37:50.975
they were talking about these people.

00:37:52.545 --> 00:37:55.515
What? Those sons of guns.

00:37:55.715 --> 00:37:57.584
She's Russian, everyone. Take a good look.

00:37:57.585 --> 00:38:01.185
If you'd like to bid, please turn on your laser pointers.

00:38:04.495 --> 00:38:05.795
Is that all, everyone?

00:38:05.895 --> 00:38:09.195
You can't pass this one up. Look at this smooth skin,

00:38:09.865 --> 00:38:10.895
Don't you want a taste?

00:38:11.195 --> 00:38:13.065
She's cute.

00:38:25.345 --> 00:38:26.815
Chief Park and Chief Choi.

00:38:27.545 --> 00:38:29.015
I'm going to need some backup.

00:38:30.915 --> 00:38:33.085
We're already geared up and ready.

00:38:38.995 --> 00:38:39.995
I'm ready too.

00:38:42.795 --> 00:38:44.835
No... What are we going to do?

00:38:51.175 --> 00:38:52.175
No, stop!

00:39:30.975 --> 00:39:32.215
She's my younger sister.

00:39:32.545 --> 00:39:34.785
- What is she saying? Come here. - She's my sister!

00:39:34.845 --> 00:39:38.485
- I won't! I'm staying with her! - Let go!

00:40:04.045 --> 00:40:06.915
Welcome, you jerks.

00:40:21.395 --> 00:40:23.395
It's okay. Don't cry.

00:40:23.795 --> 00:40:25.465
You're all going home. Don't worry.

00:40:42.415 --> 00:40:45.355
This way. Go on, head that way.

00:41:10.845 --> 00:41:11.845
Yes?

00:41:12.815 --> 00:41:13.945
Smoke?

00:41:14.885 --> 00:41:16.185
What do you mean, smoke?

00:41:19.325 --> 00:41:20.655
Got it. I'm on my way.

00:41:23.855 --> 00:41:25.125
Be careful.

00:41:32.535 --> 00:41:33.565
Watch out.

00:41:34.305 --> 00:41:35.305
It's okay.

00:41:36.075 --> 00:41:37.404
- Is that all of them? - Yes.

00:41:37.405 --> 00:41:38.475
Let's go.

00:41:47.285 --> 00:41:49.315
Who on earth are those jerks?

00:42:24.915 --> 00:42:25.955
Yes.

00:42:31.055 --> 00:42:32.325
Get them all.

00:43:12.335 --> 00:43:14.665
That was the perfect chance to take them all down.

00:43:15.405 --> 00:43:17.575
That could have been critical evidence.

00:43:18.675 --> 00:43:20.505
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

00:43:22.705 --> 00:43:24.844
You're only interested in arresting them,

00:43:24.845 --> 00:43:25.915
aren't you?

00:43:26.445 --> 00:43:27.445
What?

00:43:29.145 --> 00:43:30.515
If you had moved in,

00:43:32.015 --> 00:43:34.755
they would have cut their losses, disappeared,

00:43:35.455 --> 00:43:38.025
and taken all the unfound victims with them.

00:43:41.795 --> 00:43:43.395
I thought we were on the same side.

00:43:45.665 --> 00:43:46.665
Are we not?

00:43:47.305 --> 00:43:48.905
If our interests align,

00:43:50.535 --> 00:43:52.175
then sure, we're on the same side.

00:44:04.555 --> 00:44:06.655
That jerk is definitely hiding something.

00:44:08.055 --> 00:44:10.555
- What? - He could be playing both sides.

00:44:11.655 --> 00:44:13.695
He could just as easily team up with them,

00:44:14.165 --> 00:44:15.525
as he did with us.

00:44:18.265 --> 00:44:19.905
We need to keep an eye on him.

00:44:21.305 --> 00:44:24.705
If they took I Seo the same way they did at the port,

00:44:25.035 --> 00:44:26.475
how would we ever find her?

00:44:26.845 --> 00:44:29.445
And there's only one person who would know, isn't there?

00:44:29.745 --> 00:44:32.945
The man who doesn't even trust his own men.

00:44:33.585 --> 00:44:34.785
Matsuda Keita.

00:44:35.515 --> 00:44:37.755
We have to get inside his base, no matter what.

00:44:40.025 --> 00:44:41.825
Driver Kim, you'll be okay, right?

00:44:42.255 --> 00:44:43.595
He won't take this lying down.

00:44:43.995 --> 00:44:47.295
This all happened after I joined, so I'll be his first suspect.

00:44:52.035 --> 00:44:53.804
- Brought you a guest. - He's back.

00:44:53.805 --> 00:44:55.305
I'm sick of this old Yakuza geezer.

00:45:02.875 --> 00:45:05.315
I'll need you to have my back this time, Mr. Jang.

00:45:06.075 --> 00:45:07.585
Me? Have your back?

00:45:07.985 --> 00:45:10.085
Of course I will. Just tell me what to do.

00:45:17.525 --> 00:45:19.055
Bring them here!

00:45:23.435 --> 00:45:25.965
You too, darn it!

00:45:29.705 --> 00:45:31.375
On your feet!

00:45:43.815 --> 00:45:45.915
Regarding yesterday's incident,

00:45:47.755 --> 00:45:50.055
the only thing that's different about our organization...

00:45:51.655 --> 00:45:53.865
is the presence of you part-timers.

00:45:54.665 --> 00:45:56.165
I don't know anything.

00:45:58.195 --> 00:45:59.935
Then you'll die knowing nothing.

00:46:02.105 --> 00:46:05.075
What about you? Do you have a guilty conscience?

00:46:05.205 --> 00:46:08.645
I'm just a part-timer! Help me! Please, help me!

00:46:10.575 --> 00:46:12.645
The truth...

00:46:15.815 --> 00:46:19.015
I have a feeling the truth is pointless here.

00:46:27.465 --> 00:46:29.865
- The truth? - Right now, you're not...

00:46:30.635 --> 00:46:33.965
interested in finding the traitor.

00:46:34.435 --> 00:46:35.635
And why would I be?

00:46:35.905 --> 00:46:38.305
If I kill all of them, the traitor will die with them.

00:46:42.705 --> 00:46:43.775
Coward.

00:46:49.445 --> 00:46:52.715
You've never trusted anyone in your life. Not once.

00:46:53.385 --> 00:46:56.455
You just kill everyone before you have to trust them.

00:46:58.995 --> 00:47:01.895
That's because you're terrified of being betrayed.

00:47:03.895 --> 00:47:04.935
You should answer this.

00:47:07.035 --> 00:47:11.335
I hope you enjoyed the little gift I sent to the port yesterday.

00:47:12.905 --> 00:47:16.445
Did you really think our clan would just stand by and do nothing?

00:47:16.845 --> 00:47:17.975
Who are you?

00:47:18.515 --> 00:47:19.545
I am...

00:47:20.585 --> 00:47:23.655
the original owner of this land you're standing on.

00:47:23.955 --> 00:47:25.785
The third-generation head of the Haneshima Clan,

00:47:26.115 --> 00:47:27.755
Hoshino Masahisa!

00:47:28.655 --> 00:47:29.895
Who did you say you were again?

00:47:30.225 --> 00:47:32.255
Yesterday was just a warning.

00:47:32.895 --> 00:47:35.065
Next time, we're coming for your lives.

00:47:35.565 --> 00:47:38.994
You've got a lot of nerve for some washed-up old geezer.

00:47:38.995 --> 00:47:41.105
I dare you to say that to my face!

00:47:42.835 --> 00:47:47.005
Come find me anytime you want. I'll say it to your face all day.

00:47:50.875 --> 00:47:53.345
- Just kill them all. - Yes, sir!

00:47:53.415 --> 00:47:56.015
- Yes, sir! - I'm going with you!

00:47:58.855 --> 00:48:01.085
I'm dying to know...

00:48:01.985 --> 00:48:03.695
who it was that set me up.

00:48:27.885 --> 00:48:29.715
Darn it. Nothing's gone right lately.

00:48:30.015 --> 00:48:31.085
My goodness.

00:48:31.285 --> 00:48:33.155
You didn't use to be like this.

00:48:40.065 --> 00:48:41.365
I can't take this anymore.

00:48:43.295 --> 00:48:46.665
- Hey, you have to piss again? - Come on, move it.

00:48:46.735 --> 00:48:48.135
You drink way too much.

00:49:48.925 --> 00:49:49.935
Let's go!

00:51:22.485 --> 00:51:23.595
The Haneshima Clan.

00:51:24.525 --> 00:51:25.795
So you were all still alive?

00:51:26.395 --> 00:51:28.795
You don't even have a proper office anymore.

00:51:29.165 --> 00:51:30.835
Just this miserable dump.

00:51:31.665 --> 00:51:32.865
And you call this your office?

00:51:33.235 --> 00:51:35.065
You arrogant little punk.

00:51:36.305 --> 00:51:38.275
I won't stand for any more of your insults!

00:51:38.335 --> 00:51:40.745
And what are you going to do about it, you old man?

00:51:41.475 --> 00:51:44.145
Then I'll just have to crush you all.

00:51:44.415 --> 00:51:46.145
You've got it all wrong.

00:51:49.185 --> 00:51:51.355
Your time was over a long time ago.

00:51:52.715 --> 00:51:55.185
So just wait quietly to fade into nothing.

00:51:58.895 --> 00:52:00.025
Back in the day,

00:52:00.565 --> 00:52:02.165
when I walked these streets,

00:52:02.765 --> 00:52:04.665
no one would even dare to breathe.

00:52:06.135 --> 00:52:08.035
The moment I heard a peep,

00:52:08.835 --> 00:52:10.675
they were as good as dead.

00:52:11.075 --> 00:52:13.745
All you geezers can do is talk about the good old days.

00:52:14.945 --> 00:52:16.205
Living as beggars,

00:52:16.615 --> 00:52:20.145
you jerks will die on the street and become dog food.

00:52:20.545 --> 00:52:22.585
Hey. Tell you what. I'll give you something.

00:52:24.955 --> 00:52:26.415
Here, take it.

00:52:49.175 --> 00:52:50.845
What? It's got a hole in it.

00:53:02.625 --> 00:53:03.895
Bring it on!

00:53:17.635 --> 00:53:20.075
- Boss! - Boss!

00:53:22.475 --> 00:53:23.475
Blood...

00:53:28.285 --> 00:53:30.185
We performed the ritual of brotherhood...

00:53:33.285 --> 00:53:35.585
and pledged our loyalty.

00:53:36.825 --> 00:53:39.725
With that much blood, he's not going to make it.

00:53:41.295 --> 00:53:44.135
To go this far for someone so pathetic...

00:53:46.965 --> 00:53:49.365
I am a yakuza!

00:54:01.485 --> 00:54:04.785
I hate nothing more than someone who attacks from behind.

00:54:30.545 --> 00:54:31.615
By the way...

00:54:31.875 --> 00:54:33.245
You've been wearing those same shoes, haven't you?

00:54:35.415 --> 00:54:39.955
Don't worry about what happened. This isn't my first kill.

00:54:40.525 --> 00:54:42.685
What's one more?

00:54:44.925 --> 00:54:47.295
I owe you one. The least I can do is pay you back.

00:54:47.895 --> 00:54:51.765
There's no need. I just did what I had to do.

00:54:58.435 --> 00:55:01.775
So you're the kind of jerk who loves stabbing people in the back?

00:55:02.805 --> 00:55:05.045
- Get off me. - I've been stabbed.

00:55:08.085 --> 00:55:10.215
I told you to stop messing around with that.

00:55:10.285 --> 00:55:12.055
It was really convincing, though.

00:55:14.725 --> 00:55:16.085
So, how's it going?

00:55:16.995 --> 00:55:19.595
- I feel like I'm getting close. - Okay.

00:55:43.045 --> 00:55:44.455
Boss! I'm heading out.

00:55:45.015 --> 00:55:47.525
- Sir. - Sir.

00:56:48.485 --> 00:56:49.515
Sit.

00:57:05.835 --> 00:57:07.165
So, what do you think?

00:57:09.065 --> 00:57:11.835
It's nice. I like it.

00:57:12.605 --> 00:57:14.945
What was your boss like?

00:57:16.645 --> 00:57:19.575
He always believed in me.

00:57:20.945 --> 00:57:22.415
I figured as much.

00:57:23.285 --> 00:57:25.015
Is that what you wanted to know?

00:57:27.755 --> 00:57:32.595
You know, up until now, I've never truly trusted anyone.

00:57:34.195 --> 00:57:36.265
No matter how much I stuck to the code,

00:57:36.965 --> 00:57:39.235
I'm always the one who's betrayed.

00:57:41.535 --> 00:57:43.205
That's why I have to be the one...

00:57:45.205 --> 00:57:46.435
to betray first.

00:57:48.845 --> 00:57:51.015
Sometimes, when I find a great place to eat,

00:57:52.345 --> 00:57:54.285
I'll take a picture of my food.

00:57:55.145 --> 00:57:56.515
But then, after I've taken it,

00:57:58.385 --> 00:58:00.485
I realize I don't have anyone to send it to.

00:58:02.125 --> 00:58:05.195
Food pictures are important.

00:58:07.865 --> 00:58:09.165
Can I send them to you?

00:58:13.335 --> 00:58:17.205
Not as my subordinate, Let's be family. You and me.

00:58:21.105 --> 00:58:22.145
Family...

00:58:22.875 --> 00:58:24.645
No, I mean like sworn brothers.

00:58:25.845 --> 00:58:27.645
We'll exchange cups at the altar.

00:58:35.385 --> 00:58:37.125
You win.

00:58:38.695 --> 00:58:39.755
All right.

00:58:40.365 --> 00:58:42.125
I'll set you up with a position you deserve.

00:58:43.995 --> 00:58:48.005
So I guess the casual talk...

00:58:48.635 --> 00:58:49.665
is over now, right?

00:58:59.245 --> 00:59:00.245
Boss.

00:59:24.805 --> 00:59:26.605
What the hell are you up to?

00:59:27.475 --> 00:59:29.175
That's what I want to ask you.

00:59:29.675 --> 00:59:32.375
What's with all the following and taking pictures?

00:59:33.145 --> 00:59:35.615
So you finally decided to side with criminals?

00:59:36.015 --> 00:59:38.715
You always assume whatever suits you best.

00:59:39.585 --> 00:59:43.355
Matsuda is even throwing me a grand welcome ceremony tonight.

00:59:45.155 --> 00:59:47.225
How many guys can I put in immediately?

00:59:48.525 --> 00:59:49.525
Wait a second.

01:00:07.045 --> 01:00:10.785
I wish I could at least have a hamburger steak this weekend.

01:00:11.815 --> 01:00:15.425
For that, I just need another five bucks.

01:00:32.075 --> 01:00:33.575
I've sent out all the invitations.

01:00:36.075 --> 01:00:37.575
Living as beggars,

01:00:37.745 --> 01:00:41.415
you jerks will die on the street and become dog food.

01:00:41.585 --> 01:00:44.615
Hey. Tell you what. I'll give you something.

01:00:45.315 --> 01:00:49.455
Go hole up in a temple and die already.

01:00:49.925 --> 01:00:52.555
Give me a break!

01:01:09.705 --> 01:01:10.845
You piece of trash!

01:01:11.215 --> 01:01:12.675
What are you doing hanging around here?

01:01:13.985 --> 01:01:16.585
What, feeling nostalgic for your old turf?

01:01:17.045 --> 01:01:19.385
Your time was over a long time ago.

01:01:20.185 --> 01:01:22.655
So just wait quietly to fade into nothing.

01:01:25.755 --> 01:01:28.125
I am a yakuza!

01:02:11.635 --> 01:02:15.975
By drinking from this cup, you will seal your oath as brothers.

01:02:35.895 --> 01:02:37.535
Should I let you in on a little secret?

01:02:39.335 --> 01:02:42.335
That first time I told you to come work for me,

01:02:43.035 --> 01:02:45.105
if you had actually agreed,

01:02:45.435 --> 01:02:47.175
I probably would've killed you right then and there.

01:02:47.475 --> 01:02:48.905
It's still not too late.

01:02:58.055 --> 01:03:00.355
Boss! You need to leave!

01:03:10.095 --> 01:03:13.195
Who on earth are you guys? Hey, what's going on?

01:03:14.205 --> 01:03:16.235
You can't just barge in here! Hey!

01:03:26.945 --> 01:03:29.415
Hey, what's with all these old geezers?

01:03:29.915 --> 01:03:31.015
We are...

01:03:32.685 --> 01:03:33.985
all going to die here today.

01:03:38.725 --> 01:03:40.424
We're yakuza!

01:03:40.425 --> 01:03:42.665
- We're yakuza! - We're yakuza!

01:03:43.265 --> 01:03:47.035
We're the real Yakuza!

01:03:51.035 --> 01:03:52.105
Charge!

01:04:13.425 --> 01:04:14.665
Hurry! We need to leave!

01:04:26.105 --> 01:04:27.105
Let's go.

01:04:35.885 --> 01:04:37.185
What's with these old geezers?

01:04:41.955 --> 01:04:42.955
Gone again.

01:05:12.815 --> 01:05:15.985
Seriously, when did Driver Kim Do Gi even come up with this?

01:05:16.355 --> 01:05:17.825
Kill with a borrowed sword.

01:05:19.455 --> 01:05:23.265
Put your enemies against each other to easily get what you want.

01:05:23.665 --> 01:05:28.605
That their hope to be gangsters would be stronger than we thought.

01:05:28.905 --> 01:05:33.035
- That's what Do Gi figured. - But wait, where's Mr. Kim Do Gi?

01:05:34.305 --> 01:05:35.475
Where do you think?

01:05:36.545 --> 01:05:39.045
He's making a run for it with the boss.

01:06:30.895 --> 01:06:33.595
Where on earth did you learn to drive like this?

01:06:34.435 --> 01:06:37.975
I'm a taxi driver.

01:07:05.235 --> 01:07:07.265
The more I think about it, there's only one answer.

01:07:08.205 --> 01:07:09.565
There's a mole in the organization.

01:07:12.005 --> 01:07:14.245
I really hate those who betray.

01:07:17.815 --> 01:07:19.645
I'm glad I have someone I can count on right now.

01:07:28.985 --> 01:07:30.025
Looking for this?

01:07:37.535 --> 01:07:38.595
Kim Do Gi.

01:07:39.195 --> 01:07:41.135
Since you can't ever trust anyone,

01:07:42.735 --> 01:07:44.235
you've collected quite a stash, haven't you?

01:07:44.875 --> 01:07:45.905
Why?

01:07:47.505 --> 01:07:49.905
I was going to get you everything you wanted.

01:07:51.175 --> 01:07:53.715
I was going to give the world to you.

01:07:55.115 --> 01:07:56.745
But why?

01:07:58.355 --> 01:07:59.415
What's the reason for this?

01:08:03.755 --> 01:08:05.095
Her school break is almost over.

01:08:08.495 --> 01:08:09.865
I Seo needs to go back to school.

01:08:10.695 --> 01:08:11.695
What?

01:08:11.995 --> 01:08:13.865
She has to help out at her grandma's store,

01:08:14.505 --> 01:08:15.965
and when her school club lets out,

01:08:16.465 --> 01:08:18.235
she has to go get her favorite tteokbokki.

01:08:18.505 --> 01:08:20.805
I told you to stop speaking Korean!

01:08:21.175 --> 01:08:25.175
A piece of scum like you would never understand.

01:08:26.015 --> 01:08:27.045
Not until the day you die.

01:08:27.375 --> 01:08:29.385
Me? Die?

01:08:30.515 --> 01:08:32.185
You're the one who's going to die!

01:08:51.175 --> 01:08:53.575
You know, I've noticed something.

01:08:56.045 --> 01:08:58.515
You're not much of a fighter, are you?

01:09:22.135 --> 01:09:23.335
Aren't you curious?

01:09:23.965 --> 01:09:26.075
If you were to just disappear,

01:09:26.435 --> 01:09:28.075
would they call it a missing person case?

01:09:30.105 --> 01:09:33.075
Or just taking out the trash?

01:10:08.015 --> 01:10:11.555
Didn't I tell you? I'll betray others first.

01:10:18.625 --> 01:10:20.025
Die!

01:10:35.705 --> 01:10:37.075
Not late this time.

01:10:38.545 --> 01:10:39.545
Right?

01:10:41.115 --> 01:10:42.745
Now we're in business.

01:11:02.165 --> 01:11:03.205
I Seo.

01:11:04.475 --> 01:11:05.505
I Seo.

01:11:07.505 --> 01:11:10.045
I Seo, are you okay?

01:11:11.475 --> 01:11:12.615
It's all over now.

01:11:16.885 --> 01:11:17.915
Let's go home.

01:11:19.085 --> 01:11:21.055
Let's go home, I Seo.

01:11:31.395 --> 01:11:32.465
It's okay.

01:11:35.765 --> 01:11:36.835
You're okay now.

01:11:52.715 --> 01:11:53.715
Oh Ye Ji!

01:12:05.895 --> 01:12:06.965
I'm back.

01:12:07.965 --> 01:12:09.735
- I Seo. - Yes?

01:12:13.405 --> 01:12:14.805
Didn't you miss me?

01:12:15.345 --> 01:12:16.375
Yun I Seo.

01:12:20.345 --> 01:12:22.545
I'm so glad you're back safely.

01:12:24.285 --> 01:12:25.485
I was so scared.

01:12:58.015 --> 01:13:01.385
Driver Kim Do Gi! Don't we have one more loose end to tie up?

01:13:02.025 --> 01:13:03.885
Yes, I haven't forgotten.

01:13:11.965 --> 01:13:14.235
Who's there? What?

01:13:15.965 --> 01:13:19.235
So you're saying I should just go in now, Go Eun?

01:13:19.435 --> 01:13:21.445
Sorry. I should've told you sooner, right?

01:13:21.645 --> 01:13:23.445
What the hell is that guy mumbling about?

01:13:24.145 --> 01:13:28.785
No, it's fine. If you say the word, I'm on it.

01:13:29.545 --> 01:13:32.185
- What? Hey, I locked that door. - Just get rid of him.

01:13:33.355 --> 01:13:36.725
Talking to a brick wall? Answer me. Who on earth are you, punk?

01:13:38.255 --> 01:13:39.295
What a shame.

01:13:40.255 --> 01:13:41.895
I didn't come here to talk.

01:13:42.025 --> 01:13:44.465
Hey, you son of a gun. Do you have any idea who we are?

01:13:44.765 --> 01:13:45.965
That's exactly why I'm here.

01:14:06.115 --> 01:14:07.685
So, what about our fee?

01:14:08.385 --> 01:14:10.485
Right. The expenses must've been pretty high this time.

01:14:10.585 --> 01:14:12.955
Everything costs an arm and a leg overseas, you know?

01:14:13.095 --> 01:14:15.765
Round-trip flights, lodging, food, and car rental.

01:14:15.865 --> 01:14:19.795
And parking. Man, parking in Japan is crazy expensive.

01:14:20.065 --> 01:14:22.735
Make sure you add in the money that Yakuza guy shook us down for!

01:14:23.005 --> 01:14:25.404
And Chief Choi's fines for driving the wrong way...

01:14:25.405 --> 01:14:27.604
also came out to a pretty hefty sum.

01:14:27.605 --> 01:14:28.675
Well...

01:14:29.475 --> 01:14:33.975
That's a fortune. We can't ask a student like I Seo to pay for it.

01:14:34.215 --> 01:14:36.385
Are you crazy? Where would a student get that kind of money?

01:14:36.645 --> 01:14:39.015
- I know, right? - Don't worry.

01:14:39.815 --> 01:14:42.725
- I've already been paid in full. - Nice!

01:14:42.785 --> 01:14:44.485
- What? When? - From whom?

01:14:46.225 --> 01:14:47.795
Hey, some of the money is missing!

01:14:48.095 --> 01:14:49.965
Who touched the evidence?

01:14:50.725 --> 01:14:51.735
No one.

01:14:52.965 --> 01:14:54.395
That's all there was from the start.

01:14:54.935 --> 01:14:58.035
- The amount in this ledger... - Come one. Let's keep moving!

01:14:58.335 --> 01:14:59.335
What?

01:15:00.535 --> 01:15:01.805
We've got a long list to round up.

01:15:02.205 --> 01:15:03.205
Come on.

01:15:05.415 --> 01:15:06.415
Whatever.

01:15:10.715 --> 01:15:12.585
5283, ending service.

01:16:05.275 --> 01:16:08.045
(Taxi Driver 3)

01:16:08.305 --> 01:16:11.445
They say Manager Yang hooked a real sucker.

01:16:11.675 --> 01:16:14.914
- The last owner had a DUI... - Driver Oh!

01:16:14.915 --> 01:16:16.645
And they've taken my license plate!

01:16:16.785 --> 01:16:21.585
- This car... It hit someone. - Sir, take your car keys.

01:16:21.825 --> 01:16:23.455
I told you to take it, you punk!

01:16:23.755 --> 01:16:25.325
First, I need that car back.

01:16:25.855 --> 01:16:29.595
That's right, our boss is a lawyer who passed the Bar Exam.

01:16:29.665 --> 01:16:32.965
He's been disbarred now. For killing someone.

01:16:33.095 --> 01:16:35.505
The fact that no one took your side...

01:16:36.235 --> 01:16:38.335
means you were the one in the wrong.